node_modules/
dist/
target/
.DS_Store
*.log
# Generated TypeScript. ts-rs writes into each crate's own `bindings/` when
# TS_RS_EXPORT_DIR is unset, which any plain `cargo test` does; the app imports
# only src/bindings, and CI regenerates that before type-checking.
bindings/

# Per-developer workspace state: the model last used here, and permissions
# granted for this project only. Project skills, data recipes and notes are
# meant to be committed — the first two are instructions the agent follows,
# reviewed in a diff like anything else that decides what the software does, and
# a note is prose somebody wrote for whoever reads the repository next. A
# project note that this file swallowed would be a note nobody else ever sees,
# which is the whole of what separates it from a global one.
# Matched at any depth: a `.taurus` appears wherever the app is run from, and
# an anchored pattern silently misses `src-tauri/.taurus`.
**/.taurus/*
!**/.taurus/skills/
!**/.taurus/recipes/
!**/.taurus/notes/

# Microsoft's redistributable ConPTY, fetched by `scripts/conpty.mjs` during a
# Windows build and bundled beside the executable. Not committed: 2.2 MB of
# binaries we neither build nor own, pinned by hash in the script instead. See
# the script's header for why they are shipped at all.
src-tauri/conpty/
.ui-samples/